        "name": {
            "urdu": "",
            "punjabi": "",
            "sindhi": "",
            "pashto": "",
            "balochi": ""
        },
        "cultural_importance": "",
        "desc": "<span><b>Crotalaria burhia</b> Buch.-Ham. ex Benth. in Hook Lond. J.  2:474.  1843.  Baker in Hook.f.,Fl.Brit.Ind.2:66.1876; Cooke,Fl.Bomb. Pres. (reprint ed.) 1:311.1958; Parker, For.Fl.Punj.ed.3.124.1956; Ali in Biologia 12:26.1966.  <P><P><P><p><li><A HREF='florataxon.aspx?flora_id=5&taxon_id=250064749' TITLE='Synonym' ><i>Crotalaria</i> <i>burhia</i> var. <i>tomentosa</i>  Boiss.</A><p>A low undershrub, c. 30-60 cm tall; branches numerous, hoary with dense appressed pubescence. Leaves few, deciduous, simple, c. 0.6-2.5 cm long, c. 3-10 mm broad, oblong, obtuse, pubescent on both sides. Inflorescence a 6-12-flowered, elongated raceme. Pedicels very short; bracteoles 2. Calyx c. 8-9 mm long, pubescent, teeth lanceolate. Corolla yellow, slightly exserted. Style slightly bearded at the top. Fruit c. 8-9 mm long, c. 4 mm or less wide, hairy, 3-4-seeded.<p><p><i>Fl.Per.:</i> January-February.<p>Lectotype: Ripa Jumna, <i>Wall.</i> Cat.5386 (K-W). <p>Distribution: Pakistan (Punjab, Sind, Baluchistan); India; Afghanistan. <p><p><p><p><P></span>                        <P><!-- Key -->                        </P>                         <P>                          <span id=\"lblLowerTaxonList\"></span></P>                        <BR clear=\"all\">                        <P>&nbsp;</P>                                                <P></P>                      "
